  "label": "Noise And Bias Aware Drug",
  "related": [
    "alphafold3-amyloid-5595",
    "brain-neural-4873",
    "cellular-electron-economy-e434"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "metabolic-trait-robustness-microbial-e869",
  "summary": "New work treats measurement noise, label heterogeneity, knowledge-graph degree bias and split design as modelling targets rather than preprocessing afterthoughts.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is explicit modelling of systematic distortion in pharmacological data. DeepCINET embeds viability-assay noise into a ranking framework for cancer cell line pharmacogenomic screens; siGMA uses heteroscedastic multimodal prediction with separated aleatoric and epistemic uncertainty for chemically modified siRNA efficacy; Inverse Node Frequency applies degree-based normalisation to knowledge-graph metapath features to suppress hub bias in target-adverse event prediction. Evaluation design carries the same concern: a DrugBank description-derived DDI benchmark with four chemical-overlap holdout regimes shows molecular representation rankings invert across splits, and surrogate ADME models probe how synthetic labels across 25 endpoints transfer to experimental data, with uncertainty estimates. Complementary feature-engineering work extends drug-response prediction to site-resolved PTM states, cyclic peptide and macrocycle ADMET, spatial transcriptomic signatures, MeSH-plus-graph-topology DDI fusion, and mechanistic signalling-network synergy simulation in TRAFIKK.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
